  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "xqBkhDiVqnDQz5mM9kR/4sObIOI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:19:15.173Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Recorded as gap 7b in `sync-gaps.md`. The batch aggregator collects operations from `JOB_WRITE_READY` events into a batch before handing it to the sync manager. When a job in that window fails, `handleJobFailed` (`batch-aggregator.ts:40-55`) **deletes the pending batch and processes whatever events had already arrived** \u2014 and the failed job's operations are *silently dropped*, with no notification that the batch is incomplete.\n\nWhat makes this a defect rather than a design choice is the silence. A batch that is emitted looks identical whether or not it lost operations to a failure, so a remote applies a partial run believing it complete, and nothing downstream can tell the difference. The receiving executor renumbers arriving operations against its own head and validates no hashes, so a gap does not announce itself there either.\n\nThe operations are not lost from the origin's own log \u2014 the outbox is index-driven and a later refill can derive them again \u2014 but the batch that was emitted stands as evidence of a run that never fully happened.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/reactor/sync-gaps.md` \u2014 7. Batch Aggregator \u203a 7b (batch-aggregator.ts:40-55)\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:19:15.173Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:19:15.173Z"
    }
  },
